## From entry point to deployable assets

A bundler follows imports from one or more entry points, transforms the graph, and emits files shaped for the target runtime.



The tradeoff is additional configuration and build complexity in exchange for compatibility, optimization, and coordinated asset output.

## Benefits of using a module bundler

### Dependency management

A module bundler follows imports to resolve dependencies and include the modules the application needs in its output.

```js
// Importing a module
import { myFunction } from './myModule.js';

// Using the imported function
myFunction();
```

### Performance optimization

Bundlers can optimize a production graph through minification, code splitting, asset hashing, and sometimes tree shaking. They may combine modules to reduce request overhead, but the right chunk boundaries depend on caching, HTTP protocol, download size, and execution cost. Measure the production build instead of assuming fewer files is faster.

### Code splitting

Code splitting allows you to split your code into smaller chunks that can be loaded on demand. This can improve the initial load time of your application by only loading the necessary code.

```js
// Example of dynamic import for code splitting
import('./myModule.js').then((module) => {
  module.myFunction();
});
```

### Tree shaking

Tree shaking uses static module structure and side-effect analysis to omit code proven unused. Its effectiveness depends on module format, package metadata, side effects, and bundler configuration.

```js
// Only the used function will be included in the final bundle
import { usedFunction } from './myModule.js';
usedFunction();
```

### Hot module replacement

Hot module replacement (HMR) allows you to update modules in real-time without refreshing the entire page. This can significantly speed up the development process by providing instant feedback.

```js
if (module.hot) {
  module.hot.accept('./myModule.js', function () {
    // Handle the updated module
    const updatedModule = require('./myModule.js');
    updatedModule.myFunction();
  });
}
```

### Asset management

Module bundlers can also handle other assets like CSS, images, and fonts. This allows you to import these assets directly into your JavaScript files, making it easier to manage and optimize them.

```js
// Importing a CSS file
import './styles.css';

// Importing an image
import myImage from './image.png';
```

